    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nEXAONE-4.5 (`Exaone4_5_ForConditionalGeneration`) produces garbage for any request that contains an image on every release since #50411 (v0.29.0, v0.30.0, v0.31.0, main). Text-only requests are unaffected.\n\nRoot cause: the class inherits `supports_mm_device_do_normalize = True` from `Qwen2_5_VLForConditionalGeneration`, so `mm_device_do_normalize` defaults to on and the HF processor is told `do_rescale=False, do_normalize=False`. But `EXAONE4_5_VisionTransformer` is constructed without `input_norm`, so the inherited `Qwen2_5_VisionTransformer` uses `IdentityInputNorm` and the ViT receives raw 0–255 pixels.\n\nTwo smaller issues in the same constructor are fixed alongside, since they are the same missing wiring relative to the parent class:\n\n- `self.model_config` and `self.video_pruning_rate` are never set, but the inherited `embed_multimodal` / encoder-CUDA-graph paths read them (`AttributeError` with `--compilation-config '{\"cudagraph_mm_encoder\": true}'`).\n- The MTP drafter (`Exaone4_5MultiTokenPredictor`) builds its `Exaone4DecoderLayer` without `cache_config`, so the drafter's attention ignores `--kv-cache-dtype`.\n\n## Claims\n\n- With the fix, image requests give coherent answers and are identical to the pre-#50411 behaviour (processor-side normalisation); text-only outputs and MTP acceptance are unchanged.\n- No API change: the device-side normalisation feature stays on by default for this model, now with the correct normalisation module (`build_mm_input_norm(model_config)`), exactly as `Qwen2_5_VLForConditionalGeneration` does.\n- Users on affected releases can work around it with `--no-mm-device-do-normalize`.\n\n## Validation\n\n`LGAI-EXAONE/EXAONE-4.5-33B-FP8`, TP=2, 2× A100-SXM4-40GB, greedy, thinking off, image = the model card's `assets/exaone45_input1.jpg` (a bowl of kimchi):\n\n| | \"Describe this image in one sentence.\" | gsm8k-50 (text only) |\n|---|---|---|\n| main (default flags) | `The\\n</think>\\n</think>one\\n</think>…/or/or/or/or/or…` | 0.90 |\n| this PR (default flags) | `A person in a light blue shirt is serving freshly made kimchi from a large black bowl into a smaller black dish, …` | 0.90 |\n\nSecond prompt (\"What objects are in this image? List them.\") shows the same pattern: `/or/or/or…` before, a correct itemised list (kimchi, dark ceramic bowl, …) after.\n\n- `pre-commit` passes (ruff, mypy, typos).\n- CI: the model is 33B and not in the multimodal generation test lists; the processing test (`tests/models/multimodal/processing/test_common.py`) already covers it and still passes.\n\n## Details\n\n- `exaone4_5.py`: `EXAONE4_5_VisionTransformer.__init__` gains `input_norm` and forwards it to `Qwen2_5_VisionTransformer`; `Exaone4_5_ForConditionalGeneration.__init__` passes `input_norm=build_mm_input_norm(self.model_config)` and sets `self.model_config` / `self.video_pruning_rate` like the parent.\n- `exaone4_5_mtp.py`: pass `cache_config=vllm_config.cache_config` to the MTP decoder layer.\n\nNot in this PR (follow-ups): `Exaone4Model` lacks `EagleModelMixin` although the VLM advertises `SupportsEagle3` (asserts at load); `EXAONE4_5_VisionTransformer` builds and discards the full Qwen2.5 MHA block stack in `super().__init__` before replacing it with GQA blocks.\n\nDuplicate-work check: no open PR or issue mentions EXAONE-4.5 image output, `mm_device_do_normalize` for EXAONE, or `exaone4_5` (searched `exaone4_5`, `EXAONE-4.5`, `mm_device_do_normalize input_norm`; the closed #45071 / #42281 are different bugs).\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\nAI assistance was used while preparing this PR; I reviewed every changed line and ran all of the validation above myself.\n\n",
